-title>Coronavirus M proteins accumulate in the Golgi complex beyond the site of virion budding.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>68</volume><fpage>6523</fpage><lpage>6534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8083990</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004908-KrijnseLocker2"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krijnse-Locker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Horzinek</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rottier</surname><given-names>PJM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>O-glycosylation of the coronavirus M protein. Differential localization of sialyltransferases in N- and O-linked glycosylation.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>267</volume><fpage>14094</fpage><lpage>14101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1629209</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004908-Vennema1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vennema</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Godeke</surname><given-names>G-J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossen</surname><given-names>JWA</given-names></name><name><surname>Voorhout</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name><name><surname>Horzinek</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Nucleocapsid-independent assembly of coronavirus-like particles by coexpression of viral envelope protein genes.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>2020</fpage><lpage>2028</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8617249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004908-Narayanan1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Narayanan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Mae